# Accumulate every stdin line into a loop-carried mutable variable, then print
# the collected text once the source closes.
#
# The loop's induction extent is the source's own domain. The read of `seen`
# after the loop is a `StoreFinalRead` over the store, so the source is read
# once, by the chain that reads its values.

seen := ""
for line in stdin():
    seen := seen + line + ";"
seen
